Subject: [PATCH] djxl_fuzzer: Lower the decoder memory cap on wasm

The tracking memory manager allows the decoder 1 GiB at a time, but the wasm
heap is 512 MiB and allocations outside the decoder (the harness's own
buffers, std containers) abort when they fail. Use a 256 MiB cap on wasi.

diff --git a/tools/djxl_fuzzer.cc b/tools/djxl_fuzzer.cc
index 2389d328..e307a3df 100644
--- a/tools/djxl_fuzzer.cc
+++ b/tools/djxl_fuzzer.cc
@@ -592,7 +592,15 @@ int DoTestOneInput(const uint8_t* data, size_t size) {
   size_t max_pixels = 1 << 21;
   size_t max_total_pixels = 5 * max_pixels;
 
-  TrackingMemoryManager memory_manager{/* cap */ 1 * kGiB,
+#if defined(__wasi__)
+  // The wasm heap is 512 MiB and allocation failures outside the decoder
+  // (the harness's own buffers, std containers) abort, so keep the decoder
+  // well below it.
+  constexpr size_t kMemoryCap = kGiB / 4;
+#else
+  constexpr size_t kMemoryCap = 1 * kGiB;
+#endif
+  TrackingMemoryManager memory_manager{/* cap */ kMemoryCap,
                                        /* total_cap */ 5 * kGiB};
   const auto targets = hwy::SupportedAndGeneratedTargets();
   hwy::SetSupportedTargetsForTest(targets[getFlag(targets.size() - 1)]);
